      "intent": {
        "task": "Recognize both positive reciprocal branches and preserve the excluded zero of the absolute denominator.",
        "source_solution": "For x<0,y=-1/x>0; for x>0,y=1/x>0. Both branches approach the positive side of the vertical asymptote and approach y=0 at infinity, with no point at x=0.",
        "unit_reason": "The two half-lines and denominator domain define one complete graph task, not separate point clicks.",
        "concept_blocks": [],
        "limitations": [
          "Recognizing a complete candidate graph does not demonstrate independently constructing or sampling the graph."
        ],
        "figure_observations": [
          {
            "figure_id": "fig-choice-hard-1103a",
            "observation": "Delegated creator observation, not parent or independent approval: Actual preview defect: the 390px overflow ancestor clipped B and D in the locator screenshot. Visible A/C axes, labels and reciprocal signs are readable. Preview-only repair retained this failed image and created a complete PNG with all four quadrants pixel-checked. No second image open of this figure; final B/D preview appearance awaits the independent reviewer. Actual observed path /Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/stemrobin-182-six-3129/lemmadeck/.tmp/ld-s10y-lesson/resume182-6-3129/hard-1103-1105-FIRST/creator/attempt-03/fig-choice-hard-1103a.640.png. That observation precedes the final repair; the current final640 image has not been visually approved by the creator. Independent current-image inspection remains required."
